   "evidence": "`Pdf Flavor` is `abbrev Pdf (Flavor : Type) := Flavor \u2192 \u211d \u2192 \u211d \u2192 \u211d` (Basic.lean:32), so `comap Species.quark f + comap Species.antiquark f` is definitionally the PR's `fun i x Q2 => f (.quark i) x Q2 + f (.antiquark i) x Q2` \u2014 the PR's own `Regularity.quarkAddAntiquark` proof already simps with `Pi.add_def`. `Basic.lean` has `IsPartonDensity.comap`/`Regularity.comap`/`Assumptions.comap` (lines 232-246) and `.weight` (299-320) but no `.add`; the arguments supplied here (`add_nonneg`, `.measurable.add`, `mul_add`) are exactly the general ones and use nothing about `Species`.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Particles/Parton/PDF/ChargeConjugation.lean",
   "fix": "Add an `Add` section to `PDF/Basic.lean` alongside `Comap` and `Weight`: `IsPartonDensity.add`, `Regularity.add`, `Assumptions.add` for `f + g : Pdf \u03b9`. Then define `quarkAddAntiquark f := comap Species.quark f + comap Species.antiquark f` and derive the three lemmas from `.add` plus the existing `.comap` lemmas.",
   "issue": "`IsPartonDensity.quarkAddAntiquark`, `Regularity.quarkAddAntiquark` and `Assumptions.quarkAddAntiquark` (lines 243-260) prove closure of the three bundles for one particular sum of two pullbacks. The general fact \u2014 each bundle is closed under pointwise addition of densities over the same index \u2014 is missing, so no other combination (e.g. the flavour-summed singlet, or any `q_i + q_j`) can reuse it.",
   "line": "243"
  }
